e governing body has demonstrated its commitment to this vision with itsGolf Itfacility in Glasgow. Indoor simulators such as the relatively newCL Golf in Dumfriescontinue to proliferate, while the formerEastwood Golf Clubon the south side of Glasgow has been re-launched as a shorter 12-hole course that its owners believe better suits modern lifestyles. Retailers are responding to these changing circumstances. Adele McLean, managing director ofLivingston-based TGI Golf Partnership, says traditional clubs need to look at how they engage with this \\"new breed of golfer\\". Scottish golf apparel brandRoyal & Awesomehas gathered a following with its unique \\"loud and proud\\" designs. Discount retailerAffordable Golf, headquartered in Glasgow, is rolling out a number of initiatives in conjunction withScottish Golfwhich could include the provision of vending machines at clubs that don\'t have a\\n\\nYour task:\\n1. Rate this article on FIVE separate dimensions, each on a scale of 1-100. CRITICAL: Most stories should have MOST dimensions scoring 10-40. Only truly exceptional stories should have dimensions above 70. Be CRITICAL and use LOW scores liberally.\\n\\n   HISTORICAL INTEREST (1-100): \\n   - Scores 1-20: No historical content, just current events\\n   - Scores 21-40: Minor historical mention or local history\\n   - Scores 41-60: Some historical context\\n   - Scores 61-80: Substantial historical content, heritage sites, notable historical figures\\n   - Scores 81-100: Major historical discoveries, archaeology, preservation of national heritage\\n\\n   CULTURAL INTEREST (1-100):\\n   - Scores 1-20: No cultural content, just daily news\\n   - Scores 21-40: Minor cultural mention\\n   - Scores 41-60: Some cultural context\\n   - Scores 61-80: Substantial cultural content (traditions, language, arts)\\n   - Scores 81-100: Major cultural significance, festivals, cultural revivals\\n\\n   QUIRKY INTEREST (1-100):\\n   - Scores 1-20: Mundane, everyday news\\n   - Scores 21-40: Slightly interesting angle\\n   - Scores 41-60: Moderately interesting, some human interest\\n   - Scores 61-80: Very quirky/interesting, would make diaspora smile\\n   - Scores 81-100: Exceptionally quirky, charmingly Scottish\\n\\n   ECONOMIC IMPORTANCE (1-100):\\n   - Scores 1-20: No economic significance\\n   - Scores 21-40: Minor local economic impact\\n   - Scores 41-60: Some economic relevance\\n   - Scores 61-80: Significant economic developments diaspora might care about\\n   - Scores 81-100: Major economic significance (tourism, major industries)\\n\\n   POLITICAL IMPORTANCE (1-100):\\n   - Scores 1-20: Daily politics, local governance\\n   - Scores 21-40: Minor political note\\n   - Scores 41-60: Some political relevance\\n   - Scores 61-80: Significant political developments (devolution, independence)\\n   - Scores 81-100: Major political significance affecting Scotland\'s future\\n\\n   EXAMPLES TO GUIDE YOU:\\n   - \\"Former footballer dies aged 73\\" \\u2192 Historical=15, Cultural=20, Quirky=25, Economic=5, Political=5 (average=14 \\u2192 score 2.1)\\n   - \\"Glasgow firework ban zones\\" \\u2192 Historical=10, Cultural=15, Quirky=30, Economic=25, Political=40 (average=24 \\u2192 score 2.9)\\n   - \\"Local council decision\\" \\u2192 Historical=5, Cultural=10, Quirky=15, Economic=20, Political=35 (average=17 \\u2192 score 2.3)\\n   - \\"Woman charged after patient records accessed in NHS data breach\\" \\u2192 Historical=5, Cultural=5, Quirky=5, Economic=10, Political=15 (average=8 \\u2192 score 1.7) - CRIME/LOCAL ONLY, very low relevance\\n   - \\"Man arrested after woman found dead following flat fire\\" \\u2192 Historical=5, Cultural=5, Quirky=5, Economic=5, Political=5 (average=5 \\u2192 score 1.4) - CRIME, minimal diaspora interest\\n   - \\"Archaeological discovery at Scottish castle\\" \\u2192 Historical=90, Cultural=70, Quirky=60, Economic=50, Political=20 (average=58 \\u2192 score 5.6)\\n   - \\"Scottish language revival program\\" \\u2192 Historical=60, Cultural=95, Quirky=50, Economic=40, Political=50 (average=59 \\u2192 score 5.7)\\n\\n   SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n   - CRIME STORIES (arrests, charges, murders, fires, etc.): Score ALL dimensions 1-10. These are of minimal interest to diaspora unless they involve historical/cultural significance. Average should be 5-10 \\u2192 final score 1.4-2.0.\\n   - LOCAL-ONLY STORIES (council decisions, local infrastructure, neighborhood news): Score most dimensions 5-20 unless they have broader Scottish significance. These are routine governance that doesn\'t matter to diaspora.\\n   - ROUTINE BREAKING NEWS (sports scores, daily politics, weather reports): Score 10-30 on most dimensions unless culturally/historically significant.\\n\\n   MOST daily news stories should have MOST dimensions in the 10-40 range. Be strict and use LOW scores! Crime and local-only stories should score 1-2.\\n\\n2. Generate a brief synopsis (2-3 sentences) summarizing the key points relevant to Scottish heritage/culture from a diaspora perspective.\\n\\nProvide your assessment in JSON format:\\n{\\n    \\"historical_interest\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"cultural_interest\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"quirky_interest\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"economic_importance\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"political_importance\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"reasoning\\": \\"<brief explanation of your scores for each dimension>\\",\\n    \\"synopsis\\": \\"<2-3 sentence summary focusing on Scottish heritage/culture relevance from diaspora perspective>\\",\\n    \\"relevant\\": <true if calculated average/10 >= 6.0, false otherwise>\\n}\\n", "temperature": 0.3, "max_tokens": 500, "stream": false}'
2025-11-01 22:34:22,233 - app.llm.services - DEBUG - [REQUESTS] Raw response: {"model":"llama3.2:latest","created_at":"2025-11-01T22:34:22.230427Z","response":"Based on the article provided:\n\n1. HISTORICAL INTEREST: 40\n   - Reasoning: The article does not provide substantial historical content about Scotland's golf industry beyond its origins and its significance as an internationally recognized sport. It briefly mentions heritage but doesn't delve into significant historical figures, events, or developments.\n\n2. CULTURAL INTEREST: 55\n   - Reasoning: The article touches on cultural aspects such as the evolution of golf in Scotland and the unique designs of Scottish golf apparel brand Royal \u0026 Awesome. However, it does not provide substantial content about traditions, arts, language, or other significant cultural practices that might be of interest to a diaspora audience.\n\n3. QUIRKY INTEREST: 65\n   - Reasoning: The article includes some interesting angles, such as the development of tracking technology products by Shot Scope and the proliferation of indoor simulators like CL Golf in Dumfries. These aspects show an innovative side of Scotland's golf industry that could appeal to a diaspora audience.\n\n4. ECONOMIC IMPORTANCE: 60\n   - Reasoning: The article mentions significant economic developments, such as the provision of vending machines at clubs and the expansion of retail initiatives by Scottish Golf in conjunction with Affordable Golf. These are relevant because they involve the growth and diversification of Scotland's golf industry, which could have implications for diaspora communities interested in this aspect.\n\n5. POLITICAL IMPORTANCE: 45\n   - Reasoning: The article mentions some political relevance through its coverage of developments by the R\u0026A and the role of initiatives like Golf It facility in Glasgow. However, it does not touch on significant political events or figures affecting Scotland's future, limiting its political importance for diaspora readers.\n\n6. REASONING:\n    This score reflects a balanced assessment where the article covers various aspects but doesn't delve deeply into any one area with exceptional depth or relevance to Scottish heritage and culture from a diaspora perspective.\n\n7. SYNOPSIS:\n    The article discusses the evolving business of golf in Scotland, including advancements in technology, new formats to broaden the sport's appeal, and retail initiatives that aim to engage a wider audience. While these developments are interesting for anyone involved with golf, they might not be particularly significant from a Scottish heritage or culture perspective for diaspora readers.\n\n8. RELEVANT:\n    Calculated average: (40 + 55 + 65 + 60 + 45) / 5 = 49.6\n    Since 49.6 is below the threshold of 50, this article is not considered particularly relevant to a Scottish diaspora audience from a cultural heritage perspective.\n\n9. JSON format:\n```\n{\n    \"historical_interest\": 40,\n    \"cultural_interest\": 55,\n    \"quirky_interest\": 65,\n    \"economic_importance\": 60,\n    \"political_importance\": 45,\n    \"reasoning\": \"The article covers various aspects of Scotland's golf industry, including technological advancements and retail developments. However, it doesn't delve deeply into significant historical or cultural content that would make it highly relevant to a diaspora audience.\",\n    \"synopsis\": \"The article discusses the evolving business of golf in Scotland, covering technology, new formats, and retail initiatives aiming to engage a wider audience. While interesting for golf enthusiasts, these developments are not particularly significant from a Scottish heritage or culture perspective for diaspora readers.\",\n    \"relevant\": false\n}\n```","done":true,"done_reason":"stop","context":[128006,9125,128007,271,38766,1303,33025,2696,25,6790,220,2366,18,271,128009,128006,882,128007,271,2675,527,42118,3754,9908,369,264,27188,28948,323,7829,20846,449,264,15