y at Scottish castle\\" \\u2192 Historical=90, Cultural=70, Quirky=60, Economic=50, Political=20 (average=58 \\u2192 score 5.6)\\n   - \\"Scottish language revival program\\" \\u2192 Historical=60, Cultural=95, Quirky=50, Economic=40, Political=50 (average=59 \\u2192 score 5.7)\\n\\n   SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS:\\n   - CRIME STORIES (arrests, charges, murders, fires, etc.): Score ALL dimensions 1-10. These are of minimal interest to diaspora unless they involve historical/cultural significance. Average should be 5-10 \\u2192 final score 1.4-2.0.\\n   - LOCAL-ONLY STORIES (council decisions, local infrastructure, neighborhood news): Score most dimensions 5-20 unless they have broader Scottish significance. These are routine governance that doesn\'t matter to diaspora.\\n   - ROUTINE BREAKING NEWS (sports scores, daily politics, weather reports): Score 10-30 on most dimensions unless culturally/historically significant.\\n\\n   MOST daily news stories should have MOST dimensions in the 10-40 range. Be strict and use LOW scores! Crime and local-only stories should score 1-2.\\n\\n2. Generate a brief synopsis (2-3 sentences) summarizing the key points relevant to Scottish heritage/culture from a diaspora perspective.\\n\\nProvide your assessment in JSON format:\\n{\\n    \\"historical_interest\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"cultural_interest\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"quirky_interest\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"economic_importance\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"political_importance\\": <number 1-100>,\\n    \\"reasoning\\": \\"<brief explanation of your scores for each dimension>\\",\\n    \\"synopsis\\": \\"<2-3 sentence summary focusing on Scottish heritage/culture relevance from diaspora perspective>\\",\\n    \\"relevant\\": <true if calculated average/10 >= 6.0, false otherwise>\\n}\\n", "temperature": 0.3, "max_tokens": 500, "stream": false}'
2025-11-01 23:03:43,365 - app.llm.services - DEBUG - [REQUESTS] Raw response: {"model":"llama3.2:latest","created_at":"2025-11-01T23:03:43.363821Z","response":"Rating:\n\n{\n  \"historical_interest\": 25,\n  \"cultural_interest\": 40,\n  \"quirky_interest\": 30,\n  \"economic_importance\": 5,\n  \"political_importance\": 20\n}\n\nReasoning:\nThe article does not provide substantial historical context, but it mentions that Aberdeen University was founded in 1495. This minor historical mention is not enough to score higher.\n\nThe cultural interest is moderate because the article discusses the university's governance and staff relations, which could be of some interest to those familiar with Scottish culture and history. However, the focus on internal power struggles and lack of trust rather than traditional cultural practices or heritage sites limits its relevance.\n\nThe quirky interest is average due to the somewhat unusual topic of a \"toxic\" power struggle in an ancient university. The article does not offer any particularly unique insights or perspectives that would make it stand out as exceptionally quirky.\n\nEconomic importance is very low because there is no indication that the university's governance affects the broader Scottish economy or has significant diaspora implications.\n\nPolitical importance is relatively low because the article primarily deals with internal university politics rather than national or devolved government issues that might have an impact on Scotland.\n\nSynopsis:\nA leaked report from Aberdeen University reveals a \"toxic\" power struggle between senior management and staff, highlighting cultural and behavioral challenges. The review notes a lack of trust and poor decision-making processes, which may be of limited interest to Scottish diaspora readers unless they have personal connections to the university. The article does not provide substantial historical or cultural context relevant to Scotland's heritage or traditions.","done